== 1...d5 ==

Black stakes a claim to the centre. Their d-pawn threatens to come to d4 and unseat White's knight. 

If [[/2. d4|'''2. d4''']], that danger is prevented. The game transposes into a version of the closed game where White's knight obstructs the usual move c4. No matter: White can try a Jobava-London system (Bf4) or Richter-Veresov attack (Bg5) instead. 

[[/2. e4|'''2. e4''']] is more common, allowing 2...d4, which White answers with the manoeuvre Ne2 & Ng3.  

