== 1...e5 · Reversed Nimzowitsch ==

This position resembles a Nimzowitsch defence, 1. e4 Nc6, but colours reversed and it's White to move. Given White has an extra tempo compared to Black in the Nimzowitsch, this should be very playable. 

[[/2. d4|'''2. d4''']] exd4 3. Qxd4 plays this most like a Nimzowitsch. Because Black hasn't played ...d5 yet (contrast 1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5, where White's d-pawn is hanging) they can reply 3...Nc6 immediately. 

[[/2. e4|'''2. e4''']] transposes into the Vienna game. 

[[/2. Nf3|'''2. Nf3''']] Nc6 3. d4 is the Napoleon attack, something like the Scotch game. 

