== 1...e5 ==

1...e5 is a common, sound response, establishing control over the center after White's passive opening.

A curious variation is the [[Chess Opening Theory/1. a3/1...e5/2. h3/2...d5|Creepy Crawly Formation: Classical Defence]].

Additionally, White may choose to relinquish future hope for winning the game with the [[Chess Opening Theory/1. a3/1...e5/2. b3/2...d5/3. c3/3...Nf6/4. d3/4...Nc6/5. e3/5...Bd6/6. f3/6...O-O/7. g3|Hippopotamus Attack]], a stampede of one-square pawn moves.

