== 3. Nc3 ==
White develops a knight and prepares to play e4. Developing this knight first also keeps options open for being able to play multiple lines against the King's Indian.

The main line is [[/3...Bg7|'''3...Bg7''']]. Completing the fianchetto, Black increases pressure on the centre with their pieces (in [[w:hypermodernism (chess)|hypermodern]] style). Black allows White to continue building their centre (4. e4), while preparing their forces to attack it later. '''3...d6''' and 4...Bg7 may be played as a change in move order. 

[[/3...d5|'''3...d5''']] is a sideline, the '''Grünfeld defence'''. In order for White to play e4, they must first deal with this pawn. The main line is the exchange variation, 4. cxd5, and 4...Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 leads to a typical hypermodern position where Black plans the pawn break ...c5. 

